            <ArticleTitle>[Use of central analgesia in emergency abdominal operations].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>107-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 48 patients urgent operative interventions on organs of the abdominal cavity were performed against the background of the adequate central analgesia by phentanyl (0,02 mg/kg). The authors think the method to be inexpedient in operative interventions shorter than 60 min.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
